ound with the power of  lightning and fights with a sword and  shield combo like a garuda warrior there  are several questions that come to mind  with the fact that these blight canons  defeated the champions in combat 100  years ago  firstly the champions were all unrivaled  fighters that could each easily defeat  hordes of monsters by themselves  i know that hyrule warrior's gameplay is  probably not the most canon thing to go  by but if it is even remotely accurate  as to the actual power levels of these  champions  they were definitely at or near the  power level of link himself who later  defeats the blight ganons  secondly the blight's powers such as  thunderblight's lightning or  fireblight's overshield are clearly  copied from the champions they defeated  and those powers are shown to come from  the champions themselves not the divine  beasts as we see that they can each use  their abilities outside of the giant  machines  meaning the blights must have gotten  them directly from the champions  themselves  and thirdly in a game that focuses on  countering elements and finding  elemental weaknesses  you really expect to believe that these  blight gannons used the very same  elements that the champions were experts  with  to defeat them if anything you would  think water blight ganon was sent to  kill erbosa or thunder blight ganon was  sent to kill mifa  but we know that what happened is  actually the opposite  however there is one solution that  answers all of these questions that i  mentioned earlier  what if the blight gannons are the  champions  calamity ganon sent his malice into the  world of hyrule to capture the powerful  sheikah technologies right however a  divine beast can't just be captured and  reprogrammed the same as he did with the  guardians because a divine beast  is not automated it must be piloted so  what if  to convert the divine beasts ganon sent  the blights to actually possess  the champions making them his pilots  possession is someth